cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Preregistered Cross-Testbed Domain Shift in Industrial IDS: An OpenPLC to MaCySTe Case Study"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Rifat"
    family-names: "Kinali"
    email: "info@nauticmall.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rifatkinali/cross-testbed-industrial-ids-domain-shift"
version: "1.0.0-rc2"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A preregistered reproducible research artifact evaluating whether an
  industrial intrusion detector trained and thresholded on an OpenPLC campaign
  transfers to a held-out MaCySTe campaign. RC2 uses run-level source splits,
  twenty fixed seeds, a separate unseen benign-fault stress test, and consistent
  ensemble point and uncertainty calculations while excluding private product
  source.
keywords:
  - industrial intrusion detection
  - domain shift
  - cross-testbed evaluation
  - preregistration
  - reproducibility
  - OpenPLC
  - MaCySTe
  - maritime cybersecurity
